1
00:00:01,921 --> 00:00:03,298
Hoo, hoo!

2
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:04,337
Hi!

3
00:00:04,387 --> 00:00:06,415
It's me, Popcorn!

4
00:00:06,536 --> 00:00:11,767
Welcome to Popcorn Tales, the
cozy nest of bedtime stories.

5
00:00:12,079 --> 00:00:15,493
Hug your teddy, because
tonight's story is:

6
00:00:15,543 --> 00:00:17,415
The Headless Horseman!

7
00:00:22,014 --> 00:00:27,325
Once upon a time, in Sleepy Valley,
there was a quiet place full of golden

8
00:00:27,375 --> 00:00:30,900
leaves and a little
stream that sang softly.

9
00:00:31,566 --> 00:00:36,821
That late afternoon, the boy Nico was
walking home across the wooden bridge,

10
00:00:36,871 --> 00:00:40,299
with little owl Popcorn
perched on his shoulder.

11
00:00:40,947 --> 00:00:44,032
What a beautiful afternoon, Popcorn!

12
00:00:44,237 --> 00:00:47,818
The leaves dance in the air
like little butterflies,

13
00:00:47,868 --> 00:00:51,032
Nico said, looking at the orange sky.

14
00:00:51,651 --> 00:00:53,028
Hoo, hoo!

15
00:00:53,112 --> 00:00:55,283
That's true, little one.

16
00:00:55,392 --> 00:00:59,575
But Sleepy Valley also
keeps a very famous legend,

17
00:00:59,625 --> 00:01:02,872
Popcorn answered,
straightening her red bow.

18
00:01:03,536 --> 00:01:08,584
Nico felt a cozy little chill in his
tummy, the kind that appears when someone

19
00:01:08,634 --> 00:01:11,103
hears a gently spooky story.

20
00:01:12,228 --> 00:01:17,650
When the sun said goodbye, the trees
grew darker, and the wind began to rock

21
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:18,961
the branches.

22
00:01:19,086 --> 00:01:23,958
Nico hugged his jacket and took a
quicker little step on the wooden bridge.

23
00:01:26,848 --> 00:01:30,366
Popcorn, did you hear that
sound of hooves far away?

24
00:01:30,416 --> 00:01:33,705
Nico asked in a slightly quieter voice.

25
00:01:34,292 --> 00:01:35,681
Hoo, hoo...

26
00:01:35,977 --> 00:01:37,849
I heard it, yes.

27
00:01:38,045 --> 00:01:42,484
It sounds like someone on a horse,
coming down the valley road,

28
00:01:42,534 --> 00:01:46,184
Popcorn answered, opening her eyes wide.

29
00:01:46,816 --> 00:01:52,155
Nico's little heart beat a little faster,
but he held his hand on his friend's

30
00:01:52,205 --> 00:01:53,494
soft feather.

31
00:01:54,590 --> 00:01:59,637
Suddenly, in the middle of the pale
mist, the silhouette of a very tall

32
00:01:59,687 --> 00:02:03,254
horseman appeared, riding a quiet horse.

33
00:02:03,877 --> 00:02:06,342
But Nico opened his eyes wide:

34
00:02:06,392 --> 00:02:09,139
that horseman seemed to have no head!

35
00:02:09,764 --> 00:02:14,058
Oh, Popcorn, it's the Headless
Horseman from the legend!

36
00:02:14,414 --> 00:02:16,236
Let's hide right away!

37
00:02:16,286 --> 00:02:20,422
Nico whispered, running
behind a thick tree trunk.

38
00:02:23,321 --> 00:02:28,341
The two stayed very quiet, listening
to the horse's soft steps in the leafy

39
00:02:28,391 --> 00:02:29,591
ground.

40
00:02:32,652 --> 00:02:37,135
The little fear grew a bit, like
a long shadow on the ground.

41
00:02:38,215 --> 00:02:42,609
The horseman stopped near the
bridge and spoke in a very gentle,

42
00:02:42,659 --> 00:02:44,698
slightly sad voice.

43
00:02:45,343 --> 00:02:48,171
My pumpkin... where did
my warm little pumpkin go?

44
00:02:48,221 --> 00:02:51,884
the horseman asked,
turning his body both ways.

45
00:02:52,526 --> 00:02:57,064
Nico blinked, confused, still
hidden behind the trunk.

46
00:02:57,659 --> 00:02:59,752
He is looking for a pumpkin?

47
00:02:59,864 --> 00:03:03,076
That does not sound so scary after all,

48
00:03:03,126 --> 00:03:05,442
Nico murmured to Popcorn.

49
00:03:06,040 --> 00:03:07,417
Hoo, hoo!

50
00:03:07,526 --> 00:03:11,749
Sometimes we need to listen with
our hearts before we run away,

51
00:03:11,799 --> 00:03:14,130
Popcorn said very softly.

52
00:03:14,797 --> 00:03:19,933
The horse took a gentle step, and the
mist grew a little clearer around them.

53
00:03:21,066 --> 00:03:24,994
Popcorn gave her friend a soft
feather tap on the shoulder.

54
00:03:25,563 --> 00:03:28,112
Let's ask kindly, Nico.

55
00:03:28,241 --> 00:03:30,605
Maybe he only needs some help,

56
00:03:30,655 --> 00:03:34,305
Popcorn suggested in a brave little voice.

57
00:03:34,935 --> 00:03:38,844
Nico took a deep breath, stepped
out from behind the trunk,

58
00:03:38,894 --> 00:03:41,307
and spoke very politely.

59
00:03:41,991 --> 00:03:44,220
Hello, Mister Horseman!

60
00:03:44,454 --> 00:03:46,644
We are Nico and Popcorn.

61
00:03:46,865 --> 00:03:48,759
May we help you find your pumpkin?

62
00:03:48,809 --> 00:03:51,682
Nico asked in a firm, kind voice.

63
00:03:52,319 --> 00:03:57,436
The horseman gave a tiny jump of surprise,
and then let out a relieved little

64
00:03:57,486 --> 00:03:58,686
laugh.

65
00:03:59,037 --> 00:04:00,774
Oh, what a funny little scare!

66
00:04:00,957 --> 00:04:04,207
I am Thomas, and I lost my
pumpkin hat in the wind!

67
00:04:04,547 --> 00:04:06,904
Without it, people think I have no head,

68
00:04:06,954 --> 00:04:10,021
Thomas explained, a little embarrassed.

69
00:04:11,104 --> 00:04:15,060
The three of them began to search
together among the golden leaves,

70
00:04:15,118 --> 00:04:17,338
near the singing little stream.

71
00:04:20,249 --> 00:04:23,874
She is round, orange, and
glows a little in the dark,

72
00:04:23,924 --> 00:04:25,615
like a tiny party lantern,

73
00:04:25,665 --> 00:04:28,718
Thomas described,
looking under the bushes.

74
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:33,240
Suddenly, Popcorn pointed
with her little wing.

75
00:04:33,832 --> 00:04:35,209
Hoo, hoo!

76
00:04:35,301 --> 00:04:39,415
Look over there, resting on the
little stones by the stream!

77
00:04:39,465 --> 00:04:42,532
Popcorn announced, all excited.

78
00:04:43,162 --> 00:04:47,070
Nico ran, picked up the
pumpkin with both little hands,

79
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:48,617
and lifted it high.

80
00:04:52,216 --> 00:04:57,041
The pumpkin glowed softly, like a little
smile of light in the middle of the

81
00:04:57,091 --> 00:04:58,291
night.

82
00:04:58,987 --> 00:05:03,618
Thomas set the pumpkin back in place
as his hat, and soon a very friendly

83
00:05:03,668 --> 00:05:08,540
carved face appeared, with happy
little eyes and a wide smile.

84
00:05:09,167 --> 00:05:09,955
There!

85
00:05:10,005 --> 00:05:14,177
Now I am the Pumpkin Horseman again,
the funniest neighbor in Sleepy Valley,

86
00:05:14,227 --> 00:05:17,780
Thomas said, giving his
horse a little turn.

87
00:05:18,422 --> 00:05:23,372
Nico clapped his hands, and his little
fear turned into a warm giggle in his

88
00:05:23,422 --> 00:05:24,622
chest.

89
00:05:25,059 --> 00:05:27,156
You were not scary, Thomas!

90
00:05:27,348 --> 00:05:29,493
You were only missing your favorite hat,

91
00:05:29,543 --> 00:05:32,652
Nico said, relieved and happy.

92
00:05:33,289 --> 00:05:37,241
And you two are the bravest little
friends I have ever met on this bridge,

93
00:05:37,291 --> 00:05:40,566
Thomas answered, tipping
his pumpkin in thanks.

94
00:05:41,672 --> 00:05:45,720
The three of them crossed the bridge
together under a sky full of little

95
00:05:45,770 --> 00:05:46,970
stars.

96
00:05:53,524 --> 00:05:58,632
Popcorn straightened her red bow
and spoke in a sweet little voice.

97
00:05:59,208 --> 00:06:00,585
Hoo, hoo!

98
00:06:00,689 --> 00:06:04,592
What a lovely adventure of
little fears and friendship!

99
00:06:04,814 --> 00:06:08,514
Sometimes what looks scary
just needs a little friend,

100
00:06:08,564 --> 00:06:11,327
and fear shrinks when we ask kindly,

101
00:06:11,377 --> 00:06:12,818
Popcorn said.

102
00:06:13,451 --> 00:06:18,165
Nico waved to Thomas, who rode down
the little road lit by the glowing

103
00:06:18,215 --> 00:06:19,415
pumpkin.

104
00:06:19,864 --> 00:06:24,819
And there in Sleepy Valley,
the night grew quiet, safe,

105
00:06:24,878 --> 00:06:27,514
and full of stars for a good sleep.

106
00:06:28,833 --> 00:06:30,033
The End.

107
00:06:31,740 --> 00:06:32,453
Hoo...

108
00:06:32,503 --> 00:06:33,527
Psst!

109
00:06:33,577 --> 00:06:35,149
Are you still awake?

110
00:06:35,303 --> 00:06:37,357
Did you like tonight's story?

111
00:06:37,485 --> 00:06:42,487
Nico and Popcorn showed us that sometimes
what looks scary just needs a little

112
00:06:42,537 --> 00:06:46,283
friend, and fear shrinks
when we ask kindly.

113
00:06:46,550 --> 00:06:50,856
Good night, sleep tight, and
have the sweetest dreams.

114
00:06:51,152 --> 00:06:56,050
Grown-ups: if you enjoyed it,
please subscribe to Popcorn Tales,

115
00:06:56,100 --> 00:06:58,506
for more stories at bedtime.

116
00:06:58,809 --> 00:07:00,009
Hoo...

